In the general model structure equation $\hat{y}(t|\theta) = g(\theta, Z^{t-1})$ (1.19):
- $Z^{t-1}$ denotes {{c1::the set of past measured inputs and outputs up to time $t-1$}}
- $\theta$ denotes {{c1::the finite-dimensional parameter vector parameterizing the mapping $g$}}
- $\hat{y}(t|\theta)$ denotes {{c1::the predicted/calculated model output at time $t$ given $\theta$ and $Z^{t-1}$}}
